{"id": "EUVD-2026-67531", "enisaUuid": "b1f4ae33-6f97-3a1d-a37e-d41f465f5568", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsoc: xilinx: Fix race condition in event registration\n\nThe zynqmp_power driver registers handlers for suspend and subsystem\nrestart events using register_event(). However, the work structures\n(zynqmp_pm_init_suspend_work and zynqmp_pm_init_restart_work) used by\nthese handlers were allocated and initialized after the registration\ncall.\n\nThis created a race window where, if the firmware triggered an event\nimmediately after registration but before allocation, the callback\n(suspend_event_callback or subsystem_restart_event_callback) would\ndereference a NULL pointer in work_pending(), leading to a crash.\n\nFix this by allocating and initializing the work structures before\nregistering the events.", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:49:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07ea9081b8fefb99e2f427e0f0602a5e576cb120", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e124f7b170337563d78a7a6aa152c897d229bc39", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d349aa118ff5e4cab88424ce1b16e08edd70f8bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fb445935338405110baca8f541a2df3b4cb8d712"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x28x-mxhh-x47j", "CVE-2026-80655"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "46d0b6e4-dc43-3b49-8449-88c0b6eca140", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fcf544ac64397776a18246eba5a8ca72a47c4405 <e124f7b170337563d78a7a6aa152c897d229bc39"}, {"id": "53f9e15d-d095-3b87-823b-214f68a21427", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "77972868-20e1-3a1b-8ad1-6ec385549335", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "85323e40-c513-3b36-aec5-5b725484d188", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fcf544ac64397776a18246eba5a8ca72a47c4405 <fb445935338405110baca8f541a2df3b4cb8d712"}, {"id": "8b6e399b-4489-30af-911e-bd3079793459", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fcf544ac64397776a18246eba5a8ca72a47c4405 <07ea9081b8fefb99e2f427e0f0602a5e576cb120"}, {"id": "9f33a11f-f355-3a5f-9e28-e05dd83d016c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fcf544ac64397776a18246eba5a8ca72a47c4405 <d349aa118ff5e4cab88424ce1b16e08edd70f8bb"}, {"id": "b61a30da-81b0-3306-ba3e-6cbe05f197ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c0153678-3260-3797-a71e-eb8765c2cfe4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "f14854e0-db95-3cd0-8033-cbea8817a722", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "f7882703-1f33-321f-93ad-d665279de106", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "47ea00ad-5db7-362e-b158-30d00b904c45", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}